<p>You want your online presence to grab a potential client’s attention, whether it is a service that you are selling or a product. Your key market may be in Germany, but you may be seeking to expand into the English-speaking market. Or you may be seeking to attract international clients here in Germany. </p>

<p>That’s why you want your website to be translated into English. And you want it to read like the original text, not like a translation. </p>

<p>Language Landscapes knows that the translation of your text has a unique purpose – to communicate your line of business to new clients in a way that they can relate to and understand. </p>

<p>Translating your text, however, is only one aspect of what we do. In order to strike the right chord with your target audience, we communicate with you on a regular basis throughout the process to ensure that we are appropriately placing your message. Together, we can develop a glossary of company-specific and/or product-specific terminology. This is invaluable for achieving consistency, as well as for ensuring speedier delivery and cost effectiveness with regard to any future projects that you may entrust us with.</p>

<p>As part of our quality control process, we check that the translated content fits within your existing site design, returning your website to you in the same format. We also take care to ensure that all links are intact, tags are preserved and keywords optimally localized. </p>

